// Rule 2: Microsoft Defender exclusion added (MITRE ATT&CK T1562.001)
// Data source: Defender Operational log, Event ID 5007 (configuration changed),
// collected through the data collection rule in the WindowsEvent table.
// Why 5007 and not Sysmon: in testing, 5007 recorded exclusions added both from an
// open PowerShell session and from a new powershell.exe process. Sysmon Event 1 only
// saw the second, and this Sysmon config doesn't watch the exclusions registry key.
// Rule type: near-real-time (NRT). Sentinel runs it every minute on newly arrived
// events. It replaced a scheduled version that fired twice for one late-arriving event.
WindowsEvent
| where Channel == "Microsoft-Windows-Windows Defender/Operational"
| where EventID == 5007
| extend NewValue = tostring(EventData["New Value"]),
    OldValue = tostring(EventData["Old Value"])
// 5007 fires for many config changes (service startup, config hash, UX settings).
// Keep only additions under the Exclusions key: Paths, Extensions, Processes and so on.
// Removals leave New Value empty, so they don't match.
| where NewValue contains @"\Exclusions\"
| extend ExclusionType = extract(@"\\Exclusions\\([^\\]+)\\", 1, NewValue),
    ExcludedItem = extract(@"\\Exclusions\\[^\\]+\\(.+?) = ", 1, NewValue)
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, ExclusionType, ExcludedItem, NewValue
